Z||000000||Shaun41178||11-05-2000||02:49 AM||||There was a recent post about ported stock exhaust manifolds and who offers them.  Well I do on an exchange basis.  Here is what I offer<P>The feet are welded and then the restrictions are ground out for better flow.  Dyno results on a stock 2.8 resulted in a 8 hp gain which were tested on my Fiero.  Price for this service is only $120 plus shipping.  If you decide to keep your original manifolds there will be a $50 core charge.  I can't provide this service if everyone decides to keep their originals as I would quickly run out.<P>Options include gasket matching the exhaust ports for an extra $10 as it does take a bit longer to do this.  $7 to have the manifolds painted a high temp paint.  I can not guarantee the paint though.  I painted mine with a high temp silver and the shinnyness of the paint is gone but they are still silver in color.  Any color you want but like I said I can not gaurantee how well the paint holds up.  I would just suggest if you wanted them painted to do it yourselves but for those that don't I will do it for you.  <P>One must think of this in dollar per horsepower increase.  Gains will be anywhere from an estimated 7-10 hp based on my results.  With a 10 hp increase the dollar/hp ratio is about 12-1.  That is close to the same ratio as adding nitrous to your car.  Nitrous is around a 10-1 ratio.   This is much cheaper then adding headers or the Sprint manifolds from the Fiero Store which add about the same hp to a stock 2.8.  Improvements will also be seen with modified 2.8s, 3.1s and 3.4's alike<P>I have one set available for immediate shipping.<P>Thank You.<P><P>------------------<BR>Shaun-Toledo OH, 85 GT<BR>3.2 With nitrous<BR>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178||||reg||2
Z||000001||BAM-BAM||11-05-2000||12:14 PM||||  Shaun, You mean a set of ported stock manifolds will give you the same HP gains as the sprint headers? LMK<P> Peace, BAM OUT! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach Springs/KYB shocks and struts<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats, Carpet and headliner! MOMO Commando Steering Wheel, White Face Race Style Guages And Soon To Be More!!! YEAH BABY-YEAH||||reg||5
Z||000002||Shaun41178||11-05-2000||12:45 PM||||The gains from the ported stock exhaust manifolds will provide approximately the same hp gains as the Sprint Manifolds from the Fiero Store.  I can't say they will provide just as much hp as I have never tested the Sprint manifolds against the ported stockers but 1FST2M6 dyno tested the Chris West Headers from West Coast Fieros and I think he only picked up about 8hp or so.  I hope he sees this and posts that dyno again of the West Coast Headers as I have forgotten the exact results.<P>Gain in hp will also be proportional to a point in how well the condition of your engine is now.  If your compression in all the cylinders is down around 100, you will not see as big of a gain in hp as an engine with the compression around 150 cause the one with 100 is just not as efficient.  I am just basing my dyno gain improvements on my own experience with dyno testing ported stock exhaust manifolds but most Fieros should see approximately the same gain.<P>------------------<BR>Shaun-Toledo OH, 85 GT<BR>3.2 With nitrous<BR>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178||||reg||1
